# React Native Performance

## Lists

Use `@shopify/flash-list` (or FlatList with `getItemLayout` / `estimatedItemSize`) for long lists.

## Safe area

Use `react-native-safe-area-context` (`SafeAreaProvider`, `SafeAreaView`, `useSafeAreaInsets`).

## Re-renders

Avoid inline object and function props on heavy child trees:

```tsx
// Bad
<Card style={{ padding: 16 }} onPress={() => navigate('home')} />

// Good
const cardStyle = useMemo(() => ({ padding: 16 }), []);
const handlePress = useCallback((): void => { router.push('/'); }, []);
<Card style={cardStyle} onPress={handlePress} />
```

## Platform splits

Prefer cross-platform abstractions. Use `.ios.ts` / `.android.ts` only when abstractions fail.

## Errors

Wrap async work in try/catch; show fallback UI for network and API failures — never crash silently.
